{"id":1104,"date":"2021-01-08T23:39:21","date_gmt":"2021-01-08T23:39:21","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/?post_type=rdrcnews&#038;p=1104"},"modified":"2021-01-09T04:59:10","modified_gmt":"2021-01-09T04:59:10","slug":"re-cap-info-session-dfr-storefront-improvement-program","status":"publish","type":"rdrcnews","link":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/rdrcnews\/re-cap-info-session-dfr-storefront-improvement-program\/","title":{"rendered":"RDRC Re-Cap: Info Session Storefront Improvements"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"color: #b87614;\">January 6, 2021 Info Session: Downtown Far Rockaway Artists Commissioning Program<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">RDRC&#8217;s Info Session: DFR Storefront Improvement Program was well attended, with artists, business\/property owners, and panelist, from the Rockaway community; a special thanks to Kethia Joseph, of <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www1.nyc.gov\/assets\/sbs\/downloads\/pdf\/neighborhoods\/storefront_guide_apr20.pdf\">New York City Department of \u00a0Small Business Services (NYC SBS)<\/a><\/span> for joining us. <\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">In-Partnership with RDRC and QCA, funded by NYC SBS, DFR Artists Commissioning Program\/Storefront Improvements is a way to upgrade the Downtown Far Rockaway commercial&#8217;s visual corridors appeal, upgrading storefronts with temporary creative artwork by local Rockaway artists.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">The Storefront Improvements essential to upgrading; enhancing and creating a well-designed storefront attracting customers; highlighting local businesses; defining the community and promoting a thriving neighborhood, bringing more visibility and identity to the character of Downtown Far Rockaway, with Community Panelist experienced cultural professionals with a commitment to the development of the arts and culture in their Queens community, and panelist with knowledge of Queens communities, and expertise in an artistic discipline, arts administration, or community arts programming. Artists who present a fresh perspective by creating work that speaks to Downtown Far Rockaway Queens cultural diversity bring a more vibrant and welcoming feel to our Rockaway community.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">To learn more about Downtown Far Rockaway Storefront Improvements: Business\/Property Owner click <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1skTORrW4f54oaTpTYAM2y1KwtYH_8w7b\/view?usp=sharing\">here<\/a><\/span>, Panelist click <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1RqJKmX2JdBSpxxf9qk9aDEFgtX6uooUZ\/view?usp=sharing\">here<\/a><\/span>, and Artists click <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1-W1SA75g_-B5W-p_hkVmGgvD0ezwQq65\/view?usp=sharing\">here<\/a><\/span>.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><!--more--><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/rockawaydevrevcorp\/photos\/pcb.846647966183784\/846608739521040\/\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-1102 aligncenter\" src=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/Photo4.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"427\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/Photo4.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/Photo4-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/Photo4-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/rockawaydevrevcorp\/photos\/pcb.846647966183784\/846609012854346\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-1105 aligncenter\" src=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/01\/Photo3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"398\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\